2. Unified complexity score demoted to a post-hoc proxy (manuscript)
   - Sec. 2.1.2: difficulty tiers were assigned at design time based on
     the structural complexity of the gold SQL; the additive score
     (tables x3 + WHERE/HAVING x1 + GROUP BY x2 + EXISTS x3 + derived x3;
     thresholds 8/12/17) was the guideline used then.
     compute_unified_difficulty.py is described as a post-hoc,
     reproducible approximation of that structural-complexity criterion,
     NOT the deterministic generator of the historical labels: it agrees
     with the design-time main-evaluation labels 144/245, mismatches are
     almost all between adjacent tiers (counting-rule interpretation
     differences). Only the 25 untranslated English queries were
     machine-labeled with the script (match 25/25 by construction).

